{"toolCallId":"call_1ad52c2ac20c4a749ff796a24769d1f0","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\nSpec Folder Validation v3.0.0\n\n  Folder: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent\n  Level:  1\n  Engine: orchestrator\n\n+ FILE_EXISTS: All required files present for Level 1\n+ PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: No unfilled template placeholders found\n+ TEMPLATE_SOURCE: Template source headers present\n+ ANCHORS_VALID: Anchors well formed in 4 file(s)\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALID: Frontmatter continuity basics present\n+ FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK: All spec-doc frontmatter memory blocks are structurally valid\n+ SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY: All targeted spec-doc anchors meet the sufficiency baseline\n+ MERGE_LEGALITY: No merge plan supplied; legality check skipped\n+ CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION: No routing payload supplied; contamination check skipped\n+ POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT: No post-save payload supplied; fingerprint check skipped\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT: Graph metadata checked\nx GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY: Generated metadata integrity found 1 violation(s) (enforced)\n    - graph-metadata.json: SOURCE_FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH: source_fingerprint does not match a re-derive of the current source docs, the stored derived fields may be stale\nx GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT: Generated metadata drift found 2 drifted field(s) (enforced)\n    - description: stored 'Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh' drifted from fresh '`calculate-completeness.sh` computes and prints a completion percentage, but every successful run ends in `exit 0`'\n    - causal_summary: stored '[What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]' drifted from fresh '`calculate-completeness.sh` computes and prints a completion percentage, but every successful run ends in `exit 0`'\n+ COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER: No ephemeral comment-hygiene markers found\n+ SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED: Spec status is 'Draft', not Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\n+ STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY: status cross-doc check not applicable; one status is missing or unclassified\n    - spec.md Status=Draft classified=planned\n    - implementation-summary.md Status=<missing> classified=unknown\n+ AC_COVERAGE: Acceptance coverage gate not active for this level or lifecycle state\n+ AC_CLOSURE: Acceptance closure gate not active below Level 2\n+ TOC_POLICY: TOC policy passed: no TOC headings in non-research spec documents\n+ AI_PROTOCOLS: AI protocol check not applicable for Level 1\n+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 1; phases=3, tasks=12, stories=1, scenarios=0)\n+ FOLDER_NAMING: Folder name '001-completeness-min-percent' follows naming convention\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALUES: Frontmatter values are in the shared list\n+ SOURCE_TAGS: No [SOURCE:] path:line citations in research or review artifacts\n+ GREP_CONVENTION: Grep convention: 4 document(s) conform\n+ LEVEL_MATCH: Level consistent across all files (Level 1)\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT: children_ids matches the on-disk phase children\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY: children_ids entries all carry the packet's own identity\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE: graph-metadata.json shape validation passed\n+ METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY: metadata paths carry the scaffold marker; the packet is not filed yet\n+ DESCRIPTION_SHAPE: description.json shape validation passed\n+ NORMALIZER_LINT: No local normalizeScope*/getOptionalString declarations found outside allowed files\n+ SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY: Spec doc references, metadata, and handover targets resolve cleanly\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED: Canonical-save root-spec check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED: Canonical-save source-doc check not applicable to this folder\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED: save_lineage is present for the refreshed graph metadata\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED: Packet identity normalization drift detected (soft detector)\n    - identity=scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent\n    - identity=zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent\n+ CANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS: Description and graph freshness stay within the canonical-save slack window\n+ CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS: Continuity freshness skipped: SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS is not enabled\n    - code:not_opted_in\n+ LINKS_VALID: All wikilinks under the system-spec-kit skill resolve\n\nSummary: Errors: 2  Warnings: 0\n\nRESULT: FAILED\n\nSome of these are recomputable from the repository:\n  preview  node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent\n  apply    add --apply\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"ae8b52","exit_code":2,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_1cfcfb9469194b42be164bc34b9d3ed8","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"## 9. COMPLEXITY_MATCH\n\n**Severity:** WARNING\n**Description:** Validates that declared complexity level matches actual content metrics (user stories, phases, tasks).\n\n### Expected Ranges by Level\n\n| Level | User Stories | Phases  | Tasks     |\n| ----- | ------------ | ------- | --------- |\n| 1     | 1-2          | 2-3     | 5-15      |\n| 2     | 2-4          | 3-5     | 15-50     |\n| 3/3+  | 4-15         | 5-12    | 50-200    |\n\n### Detection Patterns\n\n| Metric       | Pattern Searched                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| User Stories | `### User Story` headers in spec.md        |\n| Phases       | `### Phase` headers in plan.md             |\n| Tasks        | `- [ ] T##` or `- [ ] TASK-` in tasks.md   |\n\n### Examples\n\n**Warning (under-scoped for Level 2):**\n```\nDeclared Level: 2\nFound: 1 user story, 2 phases, 8 tasks\nExpected: 2-4 stories, 3-5 phases, 15-50 tasks\n```\n\n**Warning (over-scoped for Level 1):**\n```\nDeclared Level: 1\nFound: 5 user stories, 6 phases, 45 tasks\nExpected: 1-2 stories, 2-3 phases, 5-15 tasks\n```\n\n### How to Fix\n\nEither adjust the declared level or modify content to match:\n\n1. **Upgrade level:** If content is complex, change `| **Level** | 1 |` to `| **Level** | 2 |`\n2. **Reduce scope:** Split complex specs into multiple smaller specs\n3. **Add content:** For sparse specs, add missing user stories, phases, or tasks\n\n---\n\n## 10. AI_PROTOCOLS\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"223272","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_225796f557d64656b86e9d7259028e1e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"53:| `PLACEHOLDER_FILLED` | ERROR    | Core files    | No unfilled template placeholders              |\n54-| `LEVEL_DECLARED`     | INFO     | spec.md       | Level explicitly stated in metadata            |\n55-| `AC_COVERAGE`        | INFO     | acceptance-criteria.md | Advisory traceability scan over each criterion's Verification cell (on by default; `SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE_ENFORCE=true` makes an under-floor result fail) |\n56-| `AC_CLOSURE`         | ERROR    | acceptance-criteria.md | Closure gate for Levels 2/3/3+: unmet criteria block a completion claim, waivers must cite a real ADR |\n57-| `CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS` | WARNING | completion claims | Opt-in strict-only completion freshness check |\n58-| `ANCHORS_VALID`      | ERROR    | spec docs with anchored templates | Anchors present, paired and not nested (adr-NNN may hold adr-NNN-*) |\n59-| `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\n60-| `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\n61-| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\n62-| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n63-| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n64-| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n87-| Duplicate criterion ids | `fail` — the tally is ambiguous |\n88-| A row citing an ADR that `decision-record.md` does not contain | `fail` — the record is the whole justification |\n89-| A packet claiming completion with an `Unmet` row | `fail` — this is the closure gate |\n90-| An `Unmet` row while the packet is still in progress | `info` — work in progress is expected to carry open criteria |\n91-| Pre-cutoff packet | `info` — grandfathered |\n92-\n93-**Waiver contract:** a criterion may only be dropped or replaced through a decision record. The Waiver cell must name `ADR-NNN`, and every ADR it names must be declared in `decision-record.md` as a heading, a bold list item or a table row, outside any code fence. `ADR-1` and `ADR-001` are the same record.\n--\n267:## 4. PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\n268-\n269-**Severity:** ERROR  \n270-**Description:** Detects unfilled template placeholders that should be replaced with actual content.\n271-\n272-### Patterns Detected\n273-\n274-| Pattern                                              | Status  | Action Required           |\n275-| ---------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------- |\n276-| `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ...]`                             | FLAGGED | Replace with actual value |\n277-| `[NEEDS_CLARIFICATION: ...]` / `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: ...]` | FLAGGED | Resolve and replace |\n278-| `[OPTIONAL: ...]`                                    | IGNORED | Optional content          |\n279-\n280-### Files Scanned\n281-\n282-- `spec.md`\n283-- `plan.md`\n284-- `tasks.md`\n285-- `acceptance-criteria.md` (if exists)\n286-- `decision-record.md` (if exists)\n287-\n288-### Excluded Paths\n289-\n290-- `**/scratch/**` - Scratch files are never scanned\n291-- `**/memory/**` - Generated continuity artifacts use different validation (ANCHORS_VALID)\n292-- `**/templates/**` - Template files are expected to have placeholders\n293-\n294-### Examples\n295-\n296-❌ **Fail:**\n297-```markdown\n298-## Metadata\n299-\n300-| Field | Value |\n301-|-------|-------|\n302-| **Type** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Feature type] |  ← FLAGGED\n303-```\n304-\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"5dacbd","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
