{"toolCallId":"call_3791c6c1cab34e5a9da11cb435d4edd0","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"21:## 1. OVERVIEW\n23:### What Is This Reference?\n32:### Core Principle\n36:### Severity Levels\n48:## 2. RULE SUMMARY\n70:### AC_CLOSURE\n97:### FRONTMATTER_VALUES\n109:### SOURCE_TAGS\n148:### Non-Breaking Completion Freshness Rollout\n166:### How to Fix `CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS`\n174:## 3. FILE_EXISTS\n179:### Required Files by Level\n191:### Implementation Summary (All Levels)\n201:### Nested Packet Changelog (Recommended for phased work)\n210:### Examples\n249:### How to Fix\n267:## 4. PLACEHOLDER_FILLED\n272:### Patterns Detected\n280:### Files Scanned\n288:### Excluded Paths\n294:### Examples\n298:## Metadata\n307:## Metadata\n314:### How to Fix\n324:## 5. LEVEL_DECLARED\n329:### Detection Method\n337:### Examples\n341:## Metadata\n350:## Metadata\n358:### How to Fix\n368:## 6. ANCHORS_VALID\n373:### What Are Anchors?\n380:### Anchor Format\n388:### Rules\n398:### Examples\n404:## Project Context\n411:## Key Decisions\n422:## ADR-001: Use JWT\n425:### Context\n438:## Open Questions\n441:### Non-Functional Requirements\n453:## Open Questions\n463:### Stack Matching Logic\n472:### How to Fix\n485:## 7. FOLDER_NAMING\n490:### Naming Rules\n499:### Examples\n516:### How to Fix\n529:## 8. FRONTMATTER_VALID\n534:### Validation Checks\n544:### Examples\n574:### How to Fix\n585:## 9. COMPLEXITY_MATCH\n590:### Expected Ranges by Level\n598:### Detection Patterns\n606:### Examples\n622:### How to Fix\n632:## 10. AI_PROTOCOLS\n637:### Required for Level 3+\n647:### Scoring\n653:### Detection Patterns\n656:## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL         ← Main section\n657:### Pre-Task Checklist           ← Component 1\n658:### Execution Rules              ← Component 2\n659:### Status Reporting Format      ← Component 3\n660:### Blocked Task Protocol        ← Component 4\n663:### Examples\n667:## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n669:### Pre-Task Checklist\n673:### Execution Rules\n679:### Status Reporting Format\n682:### Blocked Task Protocol\n686:### How to Fix\n697:## 11. LEVEL_MATCH\n702:### Consistency Checks\n710:### Required Files by Level\n719:### Examples\n739:### How to Fix\n752:## 12. GOAL DOCUMENT: DURABLE BUDGET AND BINDING\n758:### What Is Measured\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"6ef607","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_3ad30841166943eda5aa7969f4794384","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ COMPONENT: post-edit-router core (runtime-neutral policy)                ║\n// ╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣\n// ║ PURPOSE: One path-dispatch table deciding which quality checker(s) run   ║\n// ║          for an edited file, shared by the Claude PostToolUse hook and   ║\n// ║          the OpenCode plugin so the two runtimes cannot drift on policy. ║\n// ║          resolveDispatch() is a pure, side-effect-free path/string       ║\n// ║          resolver (deterministic given the same inputs); runChecks()     ║\n// ║          spawns the resolved checkers under a shared deadline and        ║\n// ║          returns bounded, redacted findings. Neither function writes to  ║\n// ║          stdout/stderr or throws -- every failure path (missing checker, ║\n// ║          non-{0,1} exit, spawn error, exhausted deadline) resolves to no ║\n// ║          finding so a bug here can never block the edit it observes.    ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n'use strict';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst { existsSync } = require('node:fs');\nconst path = require('node:path');\nconst { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// Canonical checker paths (repo-relative). Pinned here so a future move of any\n// checker script only requires a one-line update, not a per-runtime hunt.\n// Comment-hygiene = sk-code/sk-code-quality (not the older system-spec-kit/rules\n// variant); placeholders = spec/ (rules/check-placeholders.sh is sourced-only,\n// not CLI-invocable); links = rules/; frontmatter + flowchart canonical live\n// under sk-doc.\nconst CHECKER_RELATIVE_PATHS = {\n  commentHygiene: '.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-comment-hygiene.sh',\n  flowchart: '.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-diagram/scripts/validate-flowchart.sh',\n  frontmatterVersions: '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/check-frontmatter-versions.sh',\n  placeholders: '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-placeholders.sh',\n  wikilinks: '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-links.sh',\n  distStaleness: '.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh',\n};\n\nconst SOURCE_EXTENSIONS = new Set(['.ts', '.tsx', '.js', '.mjs', '.cjs', '.py', '.sh', '.bash', '.jsonc']);\nconst EXCLUDED_DIR_SEGMENTS = new Set(['dist', 'node_modules', '.git']);\nconst SPEC_DOC_BASENAMES = new Set(['spec.md', 'plan.md', 'tasks.md', 'checklist.md', 'decision-record.md']);\nconst WIKILINKS_ENABLE_ENV = 'SPECKIT_VALIDATE_LINKS';\n// Mirror frontmatter-version.mjs inScope(), so the version gate fires on exactly the\n// docs the checker validates: every doc under a skill except changelog entries, test\n// input, generated output and spec-doc examples. A runtime state dir sits beside the\n// skills and git keeps exactly one tracked doc per concern in it, the concern README,\n// ignoring every other path, so that depth alone stays versioned and the rest does not.\nconst RUNTIME_STATE_DIR = '.state';\nconst RUNTIME_STATE_README = 'README.md';\nconst VERSION_SKIPPED_DIRS = new Set([RUNTIME_STATE_DIR, 'changelog', 'scratch', 'node_modules', '.git', 'dist']);\nconst VERSION_DOC_SUBTREES = new Set(['references', 'assets', 'feature-catalog', 'manual-testing-playbook']);\nconst VERSION_TEST_DIRS = new Set(['tests', 'fixtures']);\nconst VERSION_CORPUS_DIRS = new Set(['runtime', 'benchmark', 'behavior-benchmark']);\n\nconst DEFAULT_MAX_FINDING_CHARS = 2000;\nconst DEFAULT_MAX_FINDINGS = 20;\n\n// Claude PostToolUse budget -- preserves the pre-existing Python hook's 9s\n// host timeout with an 8s per-checker cap and a 0.5s minimum worth running.\nconst CLAUDE_HOOK_BUDGET_MS = 9000;\nconst CLAUDE_CHECKER_TIMEOUT_MS = 8000;\nconst CLAUDE_MIN_CHECKER_MS = 500;\n\n// OpenCode's tool.execute.after has no host timeout wrapper, so the plugin\n// self-imposes a tighter budget to keep a slow or hung checker from ever\n// being perceived as blocking tool completion.\nconst OPENCODE_DEADLINE_MS = 4000;\nconst OPENCODE_CHECKER_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;\nconst OPENCODE_MIN_CHECKER_MS = 300;\n\n// Fallback defaults used only when a caller invokes runChecks without any of\n// the runtime-specific budgets above (e.g. a bare unit test).\nconst DEFAULT_CHECKER_TIMEOUT_MS = 8000;\nconst DEFAULT_MIN_CHECKER_MS = 300;\n\n// Redacts common secret-shaped assignments before any finding text is ever\n// logged or printed. Scoped to keyworded assignments (api_key=, token:, ...)\n// rather than any long string, so an ordinary hash or identifier in a\n// checker's stdout is not needlessly mangled.\nconst SECRET_PATTERN = /((?:api[_-]?key|access[_-]?key|secret|token|password|passwd|bearer|authorization)\\s*[:=]\\s*)['\"]?([A-Za-z0-9\\-_.]{8,})['\"]?/gi;\n\n// A scheme that names itself in front of the credential is why the assignment\n// pattern above misses both `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and a bare\n// `Bearer <token>`: the span after the keyword is the scheme word, and the\n// token sits one space further on, so the requirement for an unbroken value is\n// never met. Anchor on the scheme instead and keep it readable while only the\n// token is replaced, so a finding still says which scheme it carried.\n//\n// The 8-character length floor alone cannot tell a token from prose, since\n// \"Bearer authentication\" clears it, so the run after the scheme also has to\n// look unlike a word in one of two ways: it carries a character the ordinary\n// word alphabet lacks -- a digit or one of -._~+/= -- or it reaches at least 16\n// characters and carries an uppercase letter past its first, which is what\n// random base64 and opaque tokens do and what a merely capitalised word does\n// not. A run matching neither shape is prose and stays readable. So redaction\n// is narrower than the scheme suggests: a base64 or opaque token redacts when\n// it carries a digit or symbol or reaches 16 characters with an uppercase\n// letter past its first, while an all-lowercase run without either, such as\n// `Bearer abcdefghijklmnop`, or a merely capitalised word, stays readable by\n// design. A JWT still redacts on its dots alone. The\n// scheme word is spelled out rather than matched under the `i` flag, because\n// folding would also make the uppercase test true of a lowercase run.\nconst BEARER_SCHEME_WORD = '[Bb][Ee][Aa][Rr][Ee][Rr]';\nconst BEARER_RUN_CHARS = 'A-Za-z0-9\\\\-._~+/=';\nconst BEARER_RUN = `[${BEARER_RUN_CHARS}]`;\nconst BEARER_TOKEN_SHAPE = `[0-9\\\\-._~+/=]|(?=${BEARER_RUN}{16})${BEARER_RUN}{1,}[A-Z]`;\nconst BEARER_SCHEME_PATTERN = new RegExp(\n  `\\\\b(${BEARER_SCHEME_WORD}\\\\s+['\"]?)`\n  + `(?=${BEARER_RUN}*(?:${BEARER_TOKEN_SHAPE}))`\n  + `(${BEARER_RUN}{8,})`,\n  'g',\n);\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS -- path + scope resolution\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"17dc5f","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
